Tell FFmpeg how wide a G.726 sample is, or G.726 can only be encoded.

avc_decoder_init() hands FFmpeg a codec context carrying the channel count and
the clock rate and nothing else. That is enough for every other codec, but
FFmpeg's G.726 decoder reads the ADPCM code width out of bits_per_coded_sample
and refuses to open without it:

    c->code_size = avctx->bits_per_coded_sample;
    if (c->code_size < 2 || c->code_size > 5) {
        av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Invalid number of bits %d\n", c->code_size);
        return AVERROR(EINVAL);
    }

so every attempt to decode G.726 ends as

    ffmpeg: Invalid number of bits 0
    Error returned from libav: Invalid argument
    Error creating media decoder for codec G726-32: failed to open codec context

The encoder side works only by accident of the other direction being derivable:
g726_encode_init() computes the code width itself from bit_rate/sample_rate,
which g726_encoder_init() does set. The result is a daemon that advertises
G726-16/24/32/40, transcodes happily *into* them, and fails on the first packet
that arrives *as* one.

codec_def_t already carries the width -- bits_per_sample is 2, 3, 4 and 5 for
the four G.726 variants, which is exactly what FFmpeg wants -- so pass it
through. It is set on the ADPCM_G726 codec only, because the other decoders
either overwrite the field themselves (the PCM family) or warn about a value
they did not expect (G.722 forces it back to 8).

diff --git a/lib/avc.c b/lib/avc.c
--- a/lib/avc.c
+++ b/lib/avc.c
@@ -55,6 +55,12 @@ const char *avc_decoder_init(decoder_t *dec, const str *extra_opts) {
 	dec->avc.avcctx->sample_rate = dec->in_format.clockrate;
 	dec->avc.avcctx->time_base = (AVRational){1, dec->in_format.time_base ?: dec->in_format.clockrate};
 
+	// FFmpeg's G.726 decoder takes the ADPCM code width from this field and
+	// refuses to open without it. Unlike the encoder, it will not work the
+	// width out from the bitrate.
+	if (dec->def->avcodec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_ADPCM_G726)
+		dec->avc.avcctx->bits_per_coded_sample = dec->def->bits_per_sample;
+
 	dec->avc.avcctx->width = dec->in_format.width;
 	dec->avc.avcctx->height = dec->in_format.height;
 	//dec->avc.avcctx->pix_fmt = dec->in_format.pix_fmt;
